# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose.
#
# A pattern without a slash matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth — so a bare `supabase` also excluded lib/supabase/, and the
# deployment built without the Supabase client. Anchor everything.
/node_modules
/.next
/out
/test
/supabase
*.log
/_to_delete
/CREDENTIALS.local.md
# The print bridge runs on the till PC, not on Vercel. Nothing in the
# app imports it, so shipping it would only publish the drawer token.
/bridge
